  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0 (branch cut from upstream/main f490458a).\n\n## What changed\n\n#45's GUI scope had already landed in earlier PRs: rename, saved order and drag and drop within a setup (PR #58, v0.12.0), the Setups ribbon cell and the always-present Setups browser row (#322, `fb957ec`), and each setup's operations grouped under its own browser node (#343). What was still owed was the agent surface: `RenameOperation` and `ReorderOperation` had no MCP tool (AGENTS.md \"Commands ship with an MCP tool\"). This PR adds them, which closes #45.\n\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/order_tools.rs` (new):\n  - `rename_operation {name, new_name}`: changes the display name only. The stable key and the program position stay the same, and renaming back to the key clears the label.\n  - `reorder_operation {name, target, place: \"before\"|\"after\"}`: the drag and drop's own model. It moves an operation next to another one in the same setup, refuses a move to another setup, and answers with that setup's new order.\n  - Both resolve operations by key or display name (`edit::find_op`) and run the existing undoable commands through the session History, so each is one undo step. Every construction-time refusal (a taken name, shadowing another op's key, another setup, already in place) comes back as a tool error.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/{mod,tools}.rs`: the module is registered and its table is chained into `tools::all()`.\n- `docs/decisions/45-op-order-mcp.md`: the shape choices and what was dropped.\n\nPosting, simulation and rest-machining order semantics do not change. The tools write the same `OperationMeta.order` the browser drag writes, and `setup::operation_order` still ranks setups first. There are no project-file or post-output changes.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests in the new binary `crates/app/tests/mcp_order.rs`:\n- `rename_and_reorder_are_listed_with_their_schemas`\n- `reorder_moves_within_its_setup_one_undo_step_and_refuses_another_setup`: two setups. A move within Setup1 keeps Setup2's op last, each move is one undo/redo step, and a cross-setup move, a no-op, a bad `place` and an unknown name are each refused with the order left as it was.\n- `rename_keeps_the_key_and_the_order_and_round_trips`: the key and order are unchanged, other tools find the op by its new name, a duplicate label, another op's key and a blank name are refused, save -> open in a fresh session keeps the label and order, and undo restores the key as the name.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green - 19 app suites + lib (all `app::mcp` gate-mapped suites incl. the new `mcp_order`), 0 failed, 0.4 min; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --test mcp_order -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Pause / Home program entries (#155) can't be addressed by these tools, because the MCP surface does not expose entries yet.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill's tool table is not updated. It is a process file and would bump PROCESS_VERSION in a feature PR; its SKILL.md names `tools::list()` as the live registry.\n- No GUI change, so there are no UI or snapshot changes.\n\nChangelog: MCP gains `rename_operation` and `reorder_operation`: rename an operation's display name and move it within its setup, each one undo step, over the same commands as the browser (#45)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #45\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
